// REJECTS: Unexpected token
//
// `serverUrlDefinition:` on a DeephavenConnection. SERVER_URL_DEFINITION is declared by
// DeephavenConnectionLexerGrammar.g4:11 and consumed by NOTHING -- the parser rule that shares
// its name, `serverUrlDefinition`, consumes SERVER_URL instead. The token is dead, found
// mechanically by keywords.dead_tokens() through ANTLR's tokenVocab link, and independently
// confirmed here by running it.
//
// A dead token used as a FIELD NAME is the specific hazard: unlike a dead token that is merely
// unreachable, this one reads as documentation. A rewrite harvesting its field table from the
// lexer -- the obvious mechanical approach, and the one that gets every other field in this
// grammar right -- gains a `serverUrlDefinition:` field that upstream refuses and no protocol
// class has a slot for.
//
// The `serverUrl:` line it is replacing is otherwise unchanged, semicolon-less spelling and
// all (see ./neg-deephavenconnection-serverurl-semicolon.pure), so the field name is the only
// variable.
###Connection
DeephavenConnection fixture::neg::UrlDefinition
{
    store: fixture::neg::Store;
    serverUrlDefinition: 'dummyurl.com:12345'
    authentication: # PSK {
        psk: 'abcde';
    }#;
}
